--------------------------------------------------
External knowledge that might be helpful: 
Detailed requirements include:
- The slides must belong to the TCGA-LUAD or TCGA-LUSC collections;
- The slides must be JPEG or JPEG2000 compressed;
- The slides must be digital images and exclude non-volume ones;
- The slides must contain either normal (`17621005`) or tumor (`86049000`) tissue, identified by specific DICOM codes;
- The slides must be prepared using the "Tissue freezing medium" embedding method;

With respect to the output, it should contain the following basic metadata and attributes related to slide microscopy images. Concretely,
- digital slide ID: unique numeric identifier of a digital slide, i.e., a digital image of a physical slide;
- case ID: unique numeric identifier of the study in the context of which the ditial slide was created;
- physical slide ID: unique numeric identifier of the physical slide as prepared in the wet lab; 
- patient ID: unique numeric identifier of the patient from whose tissue the physical slide was obtained;
- collection ID: numeric or character sequence describing the dataset the physical slide is part of;
- instance ID: universally unique identifier of the DICOM instance;
- GCS URL: how to access the DICOM file;
- width/height: image width and height in pixels, respectively;
- pixel spacing: image pixel spacing in mm/px;
- compression type (either value `jpeg`, `jpeg2000`, or `other`).

And the target two labels are:
- tissue_type: either `normal` or `tumor`;
- cancer_subtype: either `luad` or `lscc`.
Sort the results according to instance ID in ascending order.
The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'IDC': {'IDC_V17': ['DICOM_ALL']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Below is a compact “road‑map” that lists the most promising columns for every logical requirement, followed by ten exploratory Snowflake SQL snippets (simple → progressively complex) that help you verify content, value ranges and nesting levels before writing the definitive extraction query.

────────────────────────
Candidate columns & their potential usage  
────────────────────────
"collection_id" or "collection_name"        : filter to ‘tcga‑luad’ or ‘tcga‑lusc’  
"Modality"                                   : keep only still–microscopy images ⇒ 'SM'  
"ImageType" (VARIANT)                        : look for the token ‘VOLUME’ (volume slides)  
"TransferSyntaxUID"                          : derive compression:  
                                               • JPEG        → 1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.50, 4.51, …  
                                               • JPEG2000    → 1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.90, 4.91  
                                               •  anything else ⇒ “other” (to be excluded)  
"SpecimenDescriptionSequence" (VARIANT)      : contains nested preparation items;  
                                               look for an item where  
                                               value ILIKE '%Tissue%freezing%medium%'  
"AnatomicRegionSequence" (VARIANT)           : holds SNOMED code values;  
                                               code ‘17621005’ → normal tissue,  
                                               code ‘86049000’ → tumor tissue  
"SeriesInstanceUID"                          : use as digital slide identifier  
"StudyInstanceUID"                           : case / study identifier  
"PatientID"                                  : patient identifier  
"SOPInstanceUID"                             : unique instance identifier  
"gcs_url"                                    : direct link to the DICOM file in GCS  
"Rows", "Columns"                            : image height & width (pixels)  
"PixelSpacing" (VARIANT)                     : pixel size in mm/px (often an array [row,col])  

Basic constant conditions you will most likely apply later
• "collection_id" IN (‘tcga‑luad’, ‘tcga‑lusc’)      -- case‑insensitive  
• "Modality" = 'SM'  
• EXISTS token ‘VOLUME’ in "ImageType"                -- volume slides  
• "TransferSyntaxUID" IN (<JPEG UIDs>, <JPEG2000 UIDs>)  
• ‘Tissue freezing medium’ mentioned somewhere in "SpecimenDescriptionSequence"  
• CodeValue IN (‘17621005’, ‘86049000’) extracted from "AnatomicRegionSequence"  

────────────────────────
Ten exploratory SQL snippets  
────────────────────────
All queries read from one table:  
IDC.IDC_V17."DICOM_ALL"   
(Remember to keep every identifier in double quotes to respect Snowflake case‑sensitivity.)

```sql
-- 1️⃣  Description: List the available collections that start with TCGA‑LU* (quick sanity check)
SELECT DISTINCT "collection_id"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17."DICOM_ALL"
WHERE "collection_id" ILIKE 'tcga-lu%';

-- 2️⃣  Description: Verify that SM modality exists in the target collections
SELECT DISTINCT "Modality"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17."DICOM_ALL"
WHERE "collection_id" IN ('tcga-luad','tcga-lusc')
  AND "Modality" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;

-- 3️⃣  Description: Show transfer‑syntax values for SM images (helps decide JPEG / JPEG2000 mapping)
SELECT DISTINCT "TransferSyntaxUID"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17."DICOM_ALL"
WHERE "collection_id" IN ('tcga-luad','tcga-lusc')
  AND "Modality" = 'SM'
LIMIT 20;

-- 4️⃣  Description: Inspect ImageType components and look for the word ‘VOLUME’
SELECT d."SOPInstanceUID",
       it.value::STRING AS "image_type_component"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17."DICOM_ALL" d,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => d."ImageType") it
WHERE d."collection_id"  IN ('tcga-luad','tcga-lusc')
  AND d."Modality"       =  'SM'
  AND it.value::STRING ILIKE '%VOLUME%'
LIMIT 20;

-- 5️⃣  Description: Peek into AnatomicRegionSequence to see available CodeValue(s)
SELECT d."SOPInstanceUID",
       ar.value:"CodeValue"::STRING      AS "code_value",
       ar.value:"CodeMeaning"::STRING    AS "code_meaning"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17."DICOM_ALL" d,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => d."AnatomicRegionSequence") ar
WHERE d."Modality" = 'SM'
  AND d."collection_id" IN ('tcga-luad','tcga-lusc')
LIMIT 20;

-- 6️⃣  Description: Quick count of slides that already expose desired SNOMED codes (normal / tumor)
SELECT ar.value:"CodeValue"::STRING AS "code_value",
       COUNT(*)                     AS "n_instances"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17."DICOM_ALL" d,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => d."AnatomicRegionSequence") ar
WHERE d."Modality"       = 'SM'
  AND d."collection_id"  IN ('tcga-luad','tcga-lusc')
  AND ar.value:"CodeValue"::STRING IN ('17621005','86049000')
GROUP BY 1
ORDER BY 1;

-- 7️⃣  Description: Explore SpecimenDescriptionSequence for the phrase ‘freezing medium’
SELECT d."SOPInstanceUID",
       sd.value AS "specimen_description_json"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17."DICOM_ALL" d,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => d."SpecimenDescriptionSequence") sd
WHERE d."Modality"      = 'SM'
  AND d."collection_id" IN ('tcga-luad','tcga-lusc')
  AND LOWER(sd.value::STRING) ILIKE '%freezing%medium%'
LIMIT 20;

-- 8️⃣  Description: Correlate compression & image‑type criteria in one shot (no tissue filter yet)
SELECT d."SOPInstanceUID",
       d."TransferSyntaxUID",
       it.value::STRING AS "image_type_component"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17."DICOM_ALL" d,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => d."ImageType") it
WHERE d."collection_id"   IN ('tcga-luad','tcga-lusc')
  AND d."Modality"        =  'SM'
  AND it.value::STRING   ILIKE '%VOLUME%'
  AND d."TransferSyntaxUID" IN ('1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.50','1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.51',
                                '1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.90','1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.91')
LIMIT 20;

-- 9️⃣  Description: Produce miniature fact table with preliminary filters (still missing embedding medium)
SELECT DISTINCT
       d."SeriesInstanceUID"  AS "digital_slide_id",
       d."StudyInstanceUID"   AS "case_id",
       d."PatientID"          AS "patient_id",
       d."SOPInstanceUID"     AS "instance_id",
       d."gcs_url",
       d."Rows"               AS "height_px",
       d."Columns"            AS "width_px",
       d."PixelSpacing"       AS "pixel_spacing_var",
       d."TransferSyntaxUID"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17."DICOM_ALL" d,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => d."ImageType") it,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => d."AnatomicRegionSequence") ar
WHERE d."collection_id" IN ('tcga-luad','tcga-lusc')
  AND d."Modality"      = 'SM'
  AND it.value::STRING ILIKE '%VOLUME%'
  AND d."TransferSyntaxUID" IN ('1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.50','1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.51',
                                '1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.90','1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.91')
  AND ar.value:"CodeValue"::STRING IN ('17621005','86049000')
LIMIT 20;

-- 🔟  Description: Full prototype query – now also requiring embedding medium = “Tissue freezing medium”
SELECT DISTINCT
       d."SeriesInstanceUID"                                            AS "digital_slide_id",
       d."StudyInstanceUID"                                             AS "case_id",
       d."InstanceNumber"                                               AS "physical_slide_id",
       d."PatientID"                                                    AS "patient_id",
       d."collection_id"                                                AS "collection_id",
       d."SOPInstanceUID"                                               AS "instance_id",
       d."gcs_url",
       d."Columns"                                                      AS "width_px",
       d."Rows"                                                         AS "height_px",
       d."PixelSpacing"                                                 AS "pixel_spacing_var",
       CASE
         WHEN d."TransferSyntaxUID" IN ('1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.50','1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.51') THEN 'jpeg'
         WHEN d."TransferSyntaxUID" IN ('1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.90','1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.91') THEN 'jpeg2000'
         ELSE 'other'
       END                                                              AS "compression_type",
       CASE WHEN ar.value:"CodeValue"::STRING = '17621005' THEN 'normal'
            WHEN ar.value:"CodeValue"::STRING = '86049000' THEN 'tumor'
       END                                                              AS "tissue_type",
       CASE WHEN d."collection_id" = 'tcga-luad'  THEN 'luad'
            WHEN d."collection_id" = 'tcga-lusc'  THEN 'lscc'
       END                                                              AS "cancer_subtype"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17."DICOM_ALL" d,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => d."ImageType")                    it,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => d."AnatomicRegionSequence")       ar,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => d."SpecimenDescriptionSequence")  sd
WHERE d."collection_id" IN ('tcga-luad','tcga-lusc')
  AND d."Modality"      = 'SM'
  AND it.value::STRING ILIKE '%VOLUME%'                                   -- volume slides
  AND d."TransferSyntaxUID" IN ('1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.50','1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.51',
                                '1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.90','1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.91') -- JPEG/J2K
  AND ar.value:"CodeValue"::STRING IN ('17621005','86049000')             -- normal / tumor
  AND LOWER(sd.value::STRING) ILIKE '%tissue%freezing%medium%'            -- embedding medium
ORDER BY d."SOPInstanceUID"
LIMIT 20;
```

Feel free to adapt token lists, nesting paths or additional JSON dereferencing once you preview actual values.  When all fields look good, remove `LIMIT` and optional exploratory columns, then save the final query as your production extractor.
